--- body ---
## Context
The routing work (tracker 1052, PRs #1262 to #1293, 2026-10-08 and 09) merged
without `/gaze`: the PRs were verified by `make check`, CI, the coders' own
proofs and spot reads, and most were written by coder sub-agents of one model
family. No review-attribution record exists for them except the Luna seat on
#1272. A whole-harness review round (ticket 1071) reads the final state, not
each diff against its ticket, so it cannot replace a per-PR review. This
ticket reviews the riskiest diffs retroactively. Sibling of 1071; do not merge
the two.

## Scope
Review each diff (`gh pr diff <N>`, or the merge commit's first-parent diff)
against the exit criteria of the ticket it closed (`tickets/closed/`), in the
shape of `/review-pr` and `/verify-gate`, one PR at a time:
- #1290 rtk hook guard: runs on every Bash call; check stdin passthrough,
  the validator's accepted forms, and a shell without `sh` on PATH.
- #1291 uv adoption: `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, CI `uv sync --frozen`,
  Makefile `RUN` wrapper; check a secretless CI box, the xdist probe order,
  the pinned `setup-uv` tag, and that `requires-python` matches reality.
- #1289 test portability: exit-77 mapping, `run_checked`, the collision gate's
  new exit 2, TMPDIR and `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` changes, the Makefile
  fallback; check that no test now passes vacuously.
- #1288 review and raid skills: the new `scripts/panel-manifest-check.py` gate
  and the manifest format change in `review-pr`; check the validator's edge
  cases and that skills still launch workers correctly.
- #1269 and #1272 decorrelation doctrine and its rewrite; #1278 deletion of
  `scripts/model_policy.py` and the `AGENTS.md` rewrite (nothing else imports
  or cites them).
- Not a PR: doudou's `/usr/local/sbin/snapshot.sh` (root-owned, tested only on a
  fake tree). Read `/var/log/snapshot.log` after the first run and confirm the
  `Excluded:` lines for `.local/share/uv-cache` and each `.venv`, and that no
  non-regenerable path was removed from a snapshot.

Each review uses at least one seat from another model family than the
orchestrator (Codex with an OpenAI model is the reachable door from Claude
Code; record `no report` and `PANEL-INTEGRITY: DEGRADED` if it cannot run),
the launch line stated for each seat, and anchors as `path:line`. Capture one
review-attribution record per reviewed PR in the roar bundle that follows.

Fixing rule. The reviewed diffs predate the first review round's fixes
(#1283, #1286, #1287, #1288, #1289, #1292), which changed some of the same
files (`rules/`, `skills/route/`, the review and raid skills, the Makefile,
the test helpers). Review each PR's own diff, but write every fix against
current `origin/main`: read what the later fixes changed in the touched
lines (`git log -p origin/main -- <path>`) and the reason in their commit
messages before editing, and do not restore text or behaviour a later fix
removed on purpose (for example the tier vocabulary, the per-skill
launch-choice sentence, the exit-77 skip mapping, the guarded hook form).
Each fix that touches a path changed by a first-round PR carries a test or a
grep that fails on the reintroduced bug. Fixes land in small PRs rebased at
every gate; 1071 starts only after they are all on `main`.

Estimated cost: about 0.7 to 1.4 USD per full review (derived from grid
prices with an assumed seat mix, not measured), so roughly 5 to 10 USD for
the seven items, plus about one author-hour to read the findings.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each listed PR has a diff-anchored review; every finding is fixed, ticketed above the severity floor, or recorded as accepted
- [ ] Each PR's closed ticket exit criteria are checked against its diff, with the result recorded
- [ ] At least one other-family seat per PR, or `no report` with `PANEL-INTEGRITY: DEGRADED` stated
- [ ] A review-attribution record exists for each reviewed PR
- [ ] doudou's first real snapshot log lines are read and reported
- [ ] Every fix was written against current `origin/main`, with the later fixes' intent checked; a fix touching a first-round path carries a regression guard
- [ ] `make check` passes on `main` after the last fix, and 1071 is unblocked
